News
====

The main functional changes in the 2.7 release are to fix the address verifier
exit-100 bug, allow the "--port" option to be used more than once, add a new
"--poll-run" option, and set better file permissions when delivering to a
maildir mailbox.

Also, it is now possible to raise or lower the logging verbosity of log messages
in a named log-group or log messages from individual filters, address verifiers
and poll runners. A positive verbosity has the effect of adding one or more
"--verbose" flags and a negative verbosity removes them. Log-group verbosities
are set with the new "--log-config" option. For filters, address verifiers and
poll runners the verbosity is set by appending modifiers such as ";v+1" or
";v-2" to the relevant option value. Log-group names include "io" for the "tx>>"
and "rx<<" log messages, so using "--log-config=io-2" will suppress these
messages even if also using "--verbose" twice.

Scripts run by E-MailRelay on Windows now have their unused standard i/o handles
explicitly opened to the null device. As a result filter scripts might behave
differently when attempting to read from standard input or write to standard
error.

The scripts for doing Windows builds and for generating documentation have been
reworked, with a shift towards cmake, Qt6, MbedTLS v3 and sphinx, and away from
doxygen.

Documentation files have been de-duplicated by standardising on the CommonMark
format. These files can be processed by "pandoc" using its "-raw_html" and
"-smart" options and by sphinx by using the MyST-Parser.

Building for Windows using v3 of MbedTLS with TLS1.3 support can now be the
default since the MbedTLS v2/v3 regression with respect to client verification
of server certificates when using TLS1.3 has finally been resolved. However,
using v3 for the Windows XP build requires some extra hooks to revert to using
CryptoAPI rather than CNG (bcrypt).

The G_LIB_SMALL optimisation is withdrawn since the same code-size benefits can
be realised using compiler/linker options. These can be conveniently activated
by passing "-z" to the "configure.sh" wrapper script. (For even smaller binaries
use "make -C unity small", as before.)

Alpine Linux packages can now be created with "make apk". This has triggered a
rework of the autoconf "make install" logic so that the template config file,
pam file, auth file, systemd unit file and sysv-init scripts are all installed
as example files. The config file is additionally installed under /etc and the
pam file is additionally installed to /etc/pam.d (e_pamdir) using no-clobber
copies that can be disabled with "--disable-install-config" (previously
"--disable-install-hook") and "--disable-install-pam" respectively. The
sysv-init script is installed to /etc/init.d only if "e_initdir" is defined
appropriately, and similarly, the systemd unit file is only installed under
/usr/lib/systemd only if "e_systemddir" is so defined. No files install under
/usr/lib/emailrelay.
